# Contributing to MATRIX

**This file is a pointer, not a guide.**

It used to be a second, conflicting contribution guide. It promised a
48-hour review, a chat, office hours and a "Three Prohibitions", and it
linked to `CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md` and to `docs/L0…L13` — none of which exist
in the repository any more. Two guides that contradict each other is the
same defect the W46 audit found in the registries, and it was resolved the
same way: one document is the authority, and the other names it.

**The canonical guide is [`CONTRIBUTING.md`](CONTRIBUTING.md).** It covers
the prerequisites, the architecture and the serving paths, how to reproduce
a known-good test scope, how to propose a research question or register a
hypothesis, how to run a benchmark, how to submit a negative result, how to
propose a domain-specific pilot, and how an external contribution is
reviewed and accepted.

The Code of Conduct is [`CODE_OF_CONDUCT`](CODE_OF_CONDUCT), the licence is
[`LICENSE`](LICENSE) (AGPL-3.0 — the only licence), and the project's
constitution is `docs-v2/governance/CONSTITUTION.md`.

The earlier text of this file is preserved in the repository's history
(`git log -- CONTRIBUTING`).
